This fixture is synthetic. It was hand-authored for the Inflight reachability
test harness and does not represent output captured from a real AWS account.

It models a minimal two-tier topology: one VPC, one subnet, two EC2
instances (an app tier and a db tier), and exactly one security-group-to-
security-group ingress rule (db tier, tcp/5432, sourced from the app tier's
security group). The field shapes were copied from the vendored real AWS
describe-* output under tests/fixtures/aws/hybrid-cloud/aws_configs/, then
simplified and rewritten with fabricated identifiers, so it loads correctly
under both Inflight's describe-dir loader and Batfish's AWS snapshot
ingestion. Every VPC id, subnet id, instance id, security group id, ENI id,
IP address, and account id in this fixture is fabricated for this purpose.

Do not treat any value in this directory as real infrastructure.
